  "findings": [
    "Generic immutableJson traversal, byte accounting and freezing account for 838/1567 (53.5%) self samples in projection-only and 794/2213 (35.9%) in authenticated read plus projection.",
    "Authenticated read additionally spends 602/2213 (27.2%) self samples in ledger JSON decoding and its object-normalizing reviver. The profile does not justify caching authority state or skipping current reads.",
    "HMAC contributes only three recorded self samples in projection-only; existing per-snapshot reference reuse already limits repeated hashing for this common-selector fixture.",
    "The unchanged candidate separately passed the isolated full acceptance benchmark. No validator, authority, transport or runtime optimization was implemented on the basis of this diagnostic. Acceptance evidence is retained separately in cartography-pilot-2026-11-06.json."
  ],
  "futureWorkOnly": {
    "candidate": "A private finalizer for the freshly constructed inventory output could avoid redundant caller-object checks and cache at most 1024 JSON-encoded string lengths per invocation.",
    "requiredInvariants": [
      "Never accept raw caller objects; remain private to the validated inventory constructor.",
      "Preserve sorted keys, null-prototype objects, deep freezing, dense arrays and negative-zero normalization.",
      "Preserve exact node, depth and escaped UTF-8 byte bounds, including the 16-byte-per-task reserve.",
      "Perform null-prototype conversion before any serialization; never invoke inherited toJSON.",
      "No cross-poll cache, no ledger read bypass and no witness, tenant, revocation or live-registration freshness change.",
      "Require differential validation against immutableJson, including Unicode, escaping, prototypes, freezing and all limit failures, before considering an implementation."
    ],
    "decision": "Deferred; the existing full acceptance gate passes unchanged."
  }
